    {
      "question": "e-7275",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "d36ecae104efe006467c92040123be794c09f462ec8756def65c095bb4e137a3",
      "new_sha256": "2ac6dcba58cf5d3e70d1eb8f64ab57c9d42d10870529d37d557a15369e65f3ea",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-7275",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{x^2+2x+1} = \\dfrac{x}{(x+1)^2}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{(x+1)^2} = \\dfrac {A}{x+1} + \\dfrac {B}{(x+1)^2}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+1)^2$ and get\n\n$$\nx= A(x+1)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A(0+1)+B \\\\ 0 & =A+B \\\\ 0 & =A-1 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{(x+1)^2} = \\dfrac {1}{x+1} - \\dfrac {1}{(x+1)^2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x+1}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{1}{x+1}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1+1|-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|0+1|)+(\\frac{1}{1+1}-\\frac{1}{0+1}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}\u20612-\\operatorname{ln}\u20611)+(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20612-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042676/example-7275.json",
          "file_sha256": "324327e87dced806cbc3e179a8e388914820956dc0677cf15a5969cead11df45"
        }
